  - name: Feature-to-Activity Attention
    type: method
    description: A novel feature extraction mechanism designed to preserve temporal ordering in video-based activity recognition. It maintains unaggregated temporal information, allowing different activities to be associated with different temporal attentions.
  - name: Tri-axial Self-Attention Encoder-Decoder
    type: method
    description: A deep learning architecture used for multi-label prediction in concurrent activity recognition. It learns independent temporal associations for different activities and predicts activity combinations.
  - name: Histogram of Oriented Gradients (HOG)
    type: method
    description: A hand-crafted feature used in traditional activity recognition, capturing the distribution of gradients in an image.
  - name: Histogram of Optical Flow (HOF)
    type: method
    description: A hand-crafted feature used in traditional activity recognition, capturing the motion information in a video sequence.
  - name: CNN-LSTM
    type: method
    description: A method that combines Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) and Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks for activity recognition, leveraging CNNs for spatial feature extraction and LSTMs for temporal association modeling.

